.policy "python-security-jwt-unverified" revision 1
.description "Verify a JSON Web Token's signature against a fixed list of algorithms before trusting its claims, and never let the token's own header choose the algorithm."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. PyJWT (`jwt.decode`, `jwt.decode_complete`) and python-jose (`jose.jwt.decode`,
// `get_unverified_claims`), resolved through imports (`authlib.jose` and a module of the run named jwt are other
// names). Outside test files it reports three shapes:
//   Unverified       claims read without checking the signature (`options={"verify_signature": False}`, a dict
//                    literal or a name bound to one; PyJWT 1's `verify=False`; python-jose `get_unverified_claims`)
//                    that the code trusts: the function is an authentication hook (DRF/Django `authenticate`, a
//                    function a FastAPI `Depends`/`Security` names, or a name like get_current_user, authenticate,
//                    user_from_token, verify_token, login_required) and reads them; they are passed to a lookup
//                    (a callee naming a user, account, member, principal or identity, a Django manager, a `get`/
//                    `filter`/`where` on a session, db, query or repository, `repo.get(claims["sub"])` included);
//                    they are assigned to an identity (`request.user`, `g.current_user`, `session[...]`); or they
//                    are returned from a function no caller of the run calls. A function of the run that returns
//                    them is followed to its callers, and each call is judged the same way (UnverifiedHelper, at
//                    the call, naming the decode's file and line).
//   HeaderAlgorithm  `algorithms=` (or the third positional argument) holds the `alg` of a header read without
//                    verification: `jwt.get_unverified_header(t)`, `json.loads` of a base64 decode, a function of the
//                    run returning one, or a parameter a caller passes one to (Netflix Lemur GHSA-r9gp-7f88-9r54);
//                    HeaderAlgorithmInline when the header is read inside the decode call itself.
//   OpenAlgorithms   a decode that pins no algorithm: python-jose `jwt.decode` without `algorithms` (or
//                    `algorithms=None`), and PyJWT `jwt.decode(token, key)` without it in a run on PyJWT 1 (the run
//                    calls `.decode()` on what `jwt.encode` returns, which only PyJWT 1's bytes allow, or its
//                    setup.py pins PyJWT below 2); `algorithms` that list `"none"` or take `get_default_algorithms()`
//                    (CVE-2022-29217); and `algorithms` mixing HMAC (`HS*`) with public-key (`RS*`, `ES*`, `PS*`,
//                    `EdDSA`) algorithms, where the token's `alg` decides how the key is used (key confusion).
//   def authenticate(self, request):
//       payload = jwt.decode(token, options={"verify_signature": False})   reported: an authentication hook
//       return User.objects.get(pk=payload["sub"]), token
//   def is_jwt(token):
//       jwt.decode(token, options={"verify_signature": False})             not reported: a format sniff
// Left alone: a function that also verifies a token, whatever name or attribute it reaches it by: any decode with
// the signature on, `super().authenticate(request)` (or `<Base>.authenticate(self, …)`, simplejwt's
// `get_validated_token`), a call of a function of the run that verifies (directly or through its callees) given the
// token, a call named verify*/validat* given it, or the issuer's userinfo/introspection endpoint (read `iss`/`kid`,
// route foreign issuers away, then verify); the token is the decode's argument, the expression a name it reads was
// bound to, or a name bound to that expression (`token = creds.credentials`). Also left alone: claims only logged,
// compared or truth-tested; a header `alg` tested with `in`/`==`/`!=` or passed to a validator-named call first (the
// same expression text, or the name it is bound to); PyJWT 2 `jwt.decode` without `algorithms` (it raises);
// `verify_exp: False` alone; test files.
// Gaps: a function that verifies one token and trusts the unverified claims of another is left alone; options built
// from a non-literal (`{"verify_signature": verify}`) or merged at runtime are not read; claims stored on an object
// and read back later are not followed; the PyJWT version is read from code only (`requirements*.txt`,
// `pyproject.toml` and `setup.cfg` are not Python documents a `.rerail` rule can read, so a pin there is not seen).
//
// Cost: every relation here starts from a decode call (or a header read) and the functions around it; nothing
// pairs two arbitrary nodes of one function. The rule includes python/ast and python/calls only, with its own
// copies of the few small helpers it needs, not lib/security's taint relations.
#include "python/ast.rerail"
#include "python/calls.rerail"

.violation Unverified(at: node, how: symbol) "This JWT's signature is unchecked and its claims {how}, so a forged token passes. Verify it with a key and fixed algorithms unless it is verified before its claims are used."
Unverified(c, how) :- ju_nosig(c), !ju_reverified(c), r = min r0 : { ju_trust(c, r0) }, ju_how(r, how).

.violation UnverifiedHelper(at: node, callee: symbol, p: symbol, l: number, how: symbol) "`{callee}` returns claims of a JWT with an unchecked signature ({p}:{l}) that {how} here. Verify the token first unless it is verified here before use."
UnverifiedHelper(c, cn, p, l, how) :- ju_src(c, _), !ju_nosig(c), !ju_reverified(c), r = min r0 : { ju_trust(c, r0) },
    ju_how(r, how), s = min s0 : { ju_src(c, s0) }, docof(s, d), doc(d, p, _), line(s, l), field(c, "function", f),
    text(f, cn).

.violation HeaderAlgorithm(at: node, p: symbol, l: number) "`algorithms` comes from the token's own unverified header ({p}:{l}), so the sender picks the check. Pass a fixed list; leave it if `alg` is tested against an allow-list first."
HeaderAlgorithm(c, p, l) :- ju_decode(c, _), o = min o0 : { ju_header_alg(c, o0) }, !within(o, c), docof(o, d),
    doc(d, p, _), line(o, l).
.violation HeaderAlgorithmInline(at: node) "`algorithms` comes from this token's own unverified header, so the sender picks the check. Pass a fixed list; leave it if `alg` is tested against an allow-list first."
HeaderAlgorithmInline(c) :- ju_decode(c, _), o = min o0 : { ju_header_alg(c, o0) }, within(o, c).

.violation OpenAlgorithms(at: node, what: symbol) "This decode {what}. Pass algorithms naming only what your key signs with; safe whenever the list holds your tokens' algorithm."
OpenAlgorithms(c, "pins no algorithms, so python-jose trusts the token's alg") :- ju_jose_open(c).
OpenAlgorithms(c, "pins no algorithms, so PyJWT 1 trusts the token's alg") :- ju_pyjwt1_open(c).
OpenAlgorithms(c, "accepts none or every algorithm PyJWT knows") :- ju_weak_algs(c), !ju_jose_open(c).
OpenAlgorithms(c, "mixes HMAC and public-key algorithms, so the token's alg picks the key's use") :-
    ju_mixed_algs(c), !ju_weak_algs(c), !ju_jose_open(c).

// ---- helpers (lib/security's, copied under this rule's prefix) ---------------------------------------------------
// ju_test_doc(d): document d is test code: a tests/test/testing directory, test_*.py, *_test(s).py, conftest.py.
.decl ju_test_doc(d: number)
ju_test_doc(d) :- path_part(d, p), (p = "tests" ; p = "test" ; p = "testing" ; p = "unittests").
ju_test_doc(d) :- file_name(d, f), (glob("test_*.py", f) ; glob("*_tests.py", f) ; glob("*_test.py", f) ;
    f = "tests.py" ; f = "test.py" ; f = "conftest.py").
// ju_arg(c, i, k, v): argument v of call c, positional index i or keyword k, without parentheses.
.decl ju_arg(c: node, i: number, k: symbol, v: node)
ju_arg(c, i, k, v) :- call_arg(c, i, k, a), unparen(a, v).
// ju_call_q(c, q): call c's callee resolves to the qualified name q.
.decl ju_call_q(c: node, q: symbol)
ju_call_q(c, q) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), sym_of(f, q).

// ---- decode calls ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ju_decode(c, lib): c, outside test code, decodes a token with PyJWT ("pyjwt") or python-jose ("jose").
.decl ju_decode_q(q: symbol, lib: symbol)
ju_decode_q("jwt.decode", "pyjwt"). ju_decode_q("jwt.api_jwt.decode", "pyjwt").
ju_decode_q("jwt.decode_complete", "pyjwt"). ju_decode_q("jwt.api_jwt.decode_complete", "pyjwt").
ju_decode_q("jose.jwt.decode", "jose").
.decl ju_decode(c: node, lib: symbol)
ju_decode(c, lib) :- call_name(c, n), (n = "decode" ; n = "decode_complete"), ju_call_q(c, q), ju_decode_q(q, lib),
    docof(c, d), !ju_test_doc(d).
// ju_token_arg(c, t): t is the token call c decodes or checks.
.decl ju_token_arg(c: node, t: node)
ju_token_arg(c, t) :- ju_maybe_src(c), ju_arg(c, 0, "", t).
ju_token_arg(c, t) :- ju_maybe_src(c), ju_arg(c, -1, k, t), (k = "jwt" ; k = "token").
// ju_splat(c): decode c passes `*args`/`**kwargs`, so an argument it seems to lack may be there.
.decl ju_splat(c: node)
ju_splat(c) :- ju_decode(c, _), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, sp, _),
    (kind(sp, "list_splat") ; kind(sp, "dictionary_splat")).

// ju_nosig(c): call c reads a token's claims without checking its signature.
.decl ju_nosig(c: node)
ju_nosig(c) :- ju_opts(c, v), kind(v, "dictionary"), child(v, p, _), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", k),
    str(k, "verify_signature"), field(p, "value", f0), unparen(f0, f), kind(f, "false").
ju_nosig(c) :- ju_opts(c, v), call_name(v, "dict"), ju_arg(v, -1, "verify_signature", f), kind(f, "false").
ju_nosig(c) :- ju_decode(c, "pyjwt"), ju_arg(c, -1, "verify", v), kind(v, "false").
ju_nosig(c) :- call_name(c, "get_unverified_claims"), ju_call_q(c, q),
    (q = "jose.jwt.get_unverified_claims" ; q = "jose.jws.get_unverified_claims"), docof(c, d), !ju_test_doc(d).
// ju_opts(c, v): v is decode c's options: the argument, or the value a name given there is bound to.
.decl ju_opts(c: node, v: node)
ju_opts(c, v) :- ju_decode(c, _), ju_arg(c, -1, "options", v).
ju_opts(c, v) :- ju_decode(c, _), ju_arg(c, 3, "", v).
ju_opts(c, v) :- ju_opts(c, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v).

// ---- unverified claims and where they go -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ju_src(c, s): call c returns claims of the unverified decode s: s itself, or a call of the run's function that
// returns them (followed through any number of such functions).
.decl ju_src(c: node, s: node)
ju_src(c, c) :- ju_nosig(c).
ju_src(k, s) :- ju_ret(g, s), call_target(k, g), docof(k, d), !ju_test_doc(d).
// ju_src_fn(c, g): g is the function around claims source c.
.decl ju_src_fn(c: node, g: node)
ju_src_fn(c, g) :- ju_src(c, _), nearest(c, g, fdef).
// ju_ret(g, s): function g returns the unverified claims of s and does not verify the token itself.
.decl ju_ret(g: node, s: node)
ju_ret(g, s) :- ju_returned(c, g), ju_src(c, s), !ju_reverified(c).
// ju_returned(c, g): function g, around c, returns the claims c returned.
.decl ju_returned(c: node, g: node)
ju_returned(c, g) :- ju_val(v, c), child(r, v, 0), kind(r, "return_statement"), nearest(r, g, fdef), ju_src_fn(c, g).

// ju_val(e, c): expression e holds the claims c returned, or a part of them: through parentheses, await,
// subscripts, attributes and method calls (`claims.get("sub")`), str()/int()/UUID()/dict() and a class built from
// them (`TokenPayload(**payload)`, `User.model_validate(claims)`), containers, f-strings, operators, conditionals,
// and the names bound to them. Each step starts from a value already found.
.decl ju_val(e: node, c: node)
ju_val(c, c) :- ju_src(c, _).
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), child(e, a, _), (kind(e, "parenthesized_expression") ; kind(e, "await") ;
    kind(e, "tuple") ; kind(e, "list") ; kind(e, "set") ; kind(e, "expression_list")).
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), field(e, "value", a), kind(e, "subscript").
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), field(e, "object", a), kind(e, "attribute").
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), field(e, "function", a), kind(e, "call"), kind(a, "attribute").
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), child(al, a, _), kind(al, "argument_list"), field(e, "arguments", al), ju_carrier(e).
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), child(sp, a, 0), kind(sp, "dictionary_splat"), child(al, sp, _), field(e, "arguments", al),
    ju_carrier(e).
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), field(kw, "value", a), kind(kw, "keyword_argument"), child(al, kw, _),
    field(e, "arguments", al), ju_carrier(e).
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), field(p, "value", a), kind(p, "pair"), child(e, p, _), kind(e, "dictionary").
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), field(i, "expression", a), kind(i, "interpolation"), child(e, i, _), kind(e, "string").
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), (field(e, "left", a) ; field(e, "right", a)),
    (kind(e, "binary_operator") ; kind(e, "boolean_operator")).
ju_val(e, c) :- ju_val(a, c), child(e, a, i), kind(e, "conditional_expression"), (i = 0 ; i = 2).
ju_val(r, c) :- ju_val(v, c), ju_bind(v, h, x), look(r, x, h), kind(r, "identifier"), r != v.
// ju_carrier(e): call e's result holds its arguments: a conversion or a class built from them.
.decl ju_carrier(e: node)
ju_carrier(e) :- call_name(e, x), (x = "str" ; x = "int" ; x = "dict" ; x = "UUID" ; x = "model_validate" ;
    x = "parse_obj" ; x = "from_dict" ; x = "load" ; match("_?[A-Z].*", x)).
// ju_bind(v, h, x): scope h binds name x to value v: `x = v`, `x := v`, `a, b = v`, `for x in v`.
.decl ju_bind(v: node, h: node, x: symbol)
ju_bind(v, h, x) :- ju_val(v, _), asg(h, x, v, _).
ju_bind(v, h, x) :- ju_val(v, _), field(a, "value", v), kind(a, "named_expression"), field(a, "name", l), text(l, x),
    nearest(a, h, fscope).
ju_bind(v, h, x) :- ju_val(v, _), field(a, "right", v), kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l),
    (kind(l, "pattern_list") ; kind(l, "tuple_pattern")), child(l, i, _), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x),
    nearest(a, h, scope).
ju_bind(v, h, x) :- ju_val(v, _), field(s, "right", v), kind(s, "for_statement"), field(s, "left", l),
    (kind(l, "identifier") ; kind(l, "pattern_list") ; kind(l, "tuple_pattern")), (i = l ; child(l, i, _)),
    kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), nearest(s, h, scope).

// ju_in_args(u, k): claim value u sits in an argument of call k.
.decl ju_in_args(u: node, k: node)
ju_in_args(u, k) :- ju_val(u, _), inside(u, k, "call"), field(k, "arguments", al), within(u, al).
// ju_logged(u): claim value u is an argument of a logging call or print.
.decl ju_logged(u: node)
ju_logged(u) :- ju_in_args(u, k), call_name(k, "print").
ju_logged(u) :- ju_in_args(u, k), call_name(k, m), (m = "debug" ; m = "info" ; m = "warning" ; m = "warn" ;
    m = "error" ; m = "exception" ; m = "critical" ; m = "log"), field(k, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, _), text(o, t),
    icontains("log", t).
// ju_read(u, c): u reads the claims c returned, outside a logging call: a name bound to them, or the call itself
// used as a value (returned, or passed on).
.decl ju_read(u: node, c: node)
ju_read(u, c) :- ju_val(u, c), kind(u, "identifier"), !field(_, "left", u), !ju_logged(u).
ju_read(c, c) :- ju_src(c, _), child(r, c, _), (kind(r, "return_statement") ; kind(r, "argument_list")), !ju_logged(c).

// ju_trust(c, rank): the function around c trusts the claims c returned: 1 it authenticates with them, 2 it looks
// a user up with them, 3 it sets the caller's identity to them, 4 it returns them and no caller of the run calls it.
.decl ju_trust(c: node, rank: number)
ju_trust(c, 1) :- ju_src_fn(c, g), ju_hook(g), ju_read(_, c).
ju_trust(c, 2) :- ju_val(u, c), ju_in_args(u, k), ju_lookup_call(k), !ju_claims_method(k).
ju_trust(c, 3) :- ju_val(rt, c), field(a, "right", rt), kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", lt),
    ju_identity_target(lt).
ju_trust(c, 4) :- ju_returned(c, g), !call_target(_, g).
.decl ju_how(rank: number, how: symbol)
ju_how(1, "authenticate the caller"). ju_how(2, "pick the user"). ju_how(3, "set the caller's identity").
ju_how(4, "are returned as trusted").

// ju_hook(g): function g, around a claims source, authenticates a request: a method named authenticate (DRF
// authentication classes, Django authentication backends), a function a FastAPI `Depends(...)`/`Security(...)`
// names, or a function whose name says so.
.decl ju_hook(g: node)
ju_hook(g) :- ju_src_fn(_, g), def_name(g, x),
    match("(?i).*(authenticat|current_user|get_current|user_from|from_token|login_required|requires_auth|(verify|validate)_(access_|id_|auth_|bearer_)?(token|jwt)).*", x).
ju_hook(g) :- ju_src_fn(_, g), def_name(g, x), ju_dep_name(x).
// ju_dep_name(x): a FastAPI `Depends(x)`/`Security(x)` (or `dependency=x`) names a function x.
.decl ju_dep_name(x: symbol)
ju_dep_name(x) :- ju_dep(e), (ju_arg(e, 0, "", a) ; ju_arg(e, -1, "dependency", a)), leaf_name(a, x).
.decl ju_dep(e: node)
ju_dep(e) :- call_name(e, n), (n = "Depends" ; n = "Security"), ju_call_q(e, q),
    (q = "fastapi.Depends" ; q = "fastapi.Security" ; q = "fastapi.params.Depends" ; q = "fastapi.params.Security").
// ju_lookup_call(k): call k, given claims, finds who the caller is: a callee naming a user, account, member,
// principal, identity or customer, a Django manager, or a `get`/`filter`/`where`-like method on a session,
// database, query or repository.
.decl ju_lookup_call(k: node)
ju_lookup_call(k) :- ju_in_args(_, k), field(k, "function", f), text(f, t), !ju_log_call(k),
    (icontains("user", t) ; icontains("account", t) ; icontains("member", t) ; icontains("principal", t) ;
     icontains("identity", t) ; icontains("customer", t) ; contains(".objects.", t)).
ju_lookup_call(k) :- ju_in_args(_, k), call_name(k, m), ju_lookup_method(m), field(k, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, _),
    leaf_name(o, x), (icontains("session", x) ; x = "db" ; icontains("query", x) ; icontains("repo", x) ;
    x = "objects" ; x = "crud").
.decl ju_log_call(k: node)
ju_log_call(k) :- ju_in_args(_, k), ju_logged_call(k).
.decl ju_logged_call(k: node)
ju_logged_call(k) :- ju_in_args(u, k), ju_logged(u).
.decl ju_lookup_method(m: symbol)
ju_lookup_method("get"). ju_lookup_method("filter"). ju_lookup_method("filter_by"). ju_lookup_method("where").
ju_lookup_method("get_or_404"). ju_lookup_method("one"). ju_lookup_method("first"). ju_lookup_method("scalar").
ju_lookup_method("find_one"). ju_lookup_method("execute"). ju_lookup_method("exec"). ju_lookup_method("aget").
// ju_claims_method(k): k is a method call on the claims themselves (`claims.get("sub")`).
.decl ju_claims_method(k: node)
ju_claims_method(k) :- ju_in_args(_, k), field(k, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, _), ju_val(o, _).
// ju_identity_target(l): assignment target l holds who the caller is: an attribute naming a user, principal,
// identity, account or claims (`request.user`, `g.current_user`, `request.state.claims`), or a session key.
.decl ju_identity_target(l: node)
ju_identity_target(l) :- ju_asg_left(l), attr_of(l, _, n), (icontains("user", n) ; icontains("principal", n) ;
    icontains("identity", n) ; icontains("account", n) ; n = "claims" ; n = "auth").
ju_identity_target(l) :- ju_asg_left(l), kind(l, "subscript"), field(l, "value", v), text(v, t), icontains("session", t).
// ju_asg_left(l): l is the target of an assignment of claims.
.decl ju_asg_left(l: node)
ju_asg_left(l) :- ju_val(rt, _), field(a, "right", rt), kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l).

// ---- re-verification ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ju_maybe_src(c): c may return unverified claims (a superset of ju_src, without its recursion through
// ju_reverified): an unverified decode, or a call of a function that holds one, directly or through its callees.
.decl ju_maybe_src(c: node)
ju_maybe_src(c) :- ju_nosig(c).
ju_maybe_src(k) :- ju_msrc_fn(_, g), call_target(k, g).
.decl ju_msrc_fn(c: node, g: node)
ju_msrc_fn(c, g) :- ju_maybe_src(c), nearest(c, g, fdef).
// ju_reverified(c): the function around c also verifies the token. Reading `iss` or `kid` to pick the key, or to
// route a foreign issuer away, is then fine.
.decl ju_reverified(c: node)
ju_reverified(c) :- ju_msrc_fn(c, g), ju_verifies(g).
ju_reverified(c) :- ju_msrc_fn(c, g), ju_tok(c, tt), ju_verify_call(g, tt).
// ju_verifies(g): function g, around a claims source, verifies a token whatever expression holds it: a decode with
// the signature on, the parent's authentication (`super().authenticate(request)`, `Base.authenticate(self, …)`,
// simplejwt's `get_validated_token`), or the issuer's userinfo/introspection endpoint, which rejects a forged token.
.decl ju_verifies(g: node)
ju_verifies(g) :- ju_decode(c, _), !ju_nosig(c), nearest(c, g, fdef).
ju_verifies(g) :- ju_msrc_fn(_, g), ju_call_in(g, k), call_name(k, n), ju_parent_auth(k, g, n).
ju_verifies(g) :- ju_msrc_fn(_, g), ju_call_in(g, k), call_name(k, n), (icontains("userinfo", n) ; icontains("introspect", n)).
ju_verifies(g) :- ju_msrc_fn(_, g), ju_call_in(g, k), call_name(k, "get_validated_token").
// ju_call_in(g, k): call k is in function g, a function around a claims source.
.decl ju_call_in(g: node, k: node)
ju_call_in(g, k) :- ju_msrc_fn(_, g), kind(k, "call"), nearest(k, g, fdef).
// ju_parent_auth(k, g, n): call k, named n, in method g runs the parent class's authentication: `super().n(…)` or
// `Base.n(self, …)` with Base a base of g's class, n naming authenticate.
.decl ju_parent_auth(k: node, g: node, n: symbol)
ju_parent_auth(k, g, n) :- ju_call_in(g, k), call_name(k, n), icontains("authenticate", n), field(k, "function", f),
    attr_of(f, o, _), kind(o, "call"), call_name(o, "super").
ju_parent_auth(k, g, n) :- ju_call_in(g, k), call_name(k, n), icontains("authenticate", n), field(k, "function", f),
    attr_of(f, o, _), leaf_name(o, b), nearest(g, cls, scope), kind(cls, "class_definition"), base_name(cls, b).
// ju_verify_call(g, tt): a call in g verifies the argument whose text is tt: a call named verify*/validat* (not
// unverif*), or a call of a function of the run that verifies, directly or through its callees.
.decl ju_verify_call(g: node, tt: symbol)
ju_verify_call(g, tt) :- ju_call_in(g, k), call_name(k, n), (icontains("verif", n) ; icontains("validat", n)),
    !icontains("unverif", n), ju_arg(k, _, _, t), text(t, tt).
ju_verify_call(g, tt) :- ju_call_in(g, k), call_target(k, h), ju_verify_fn(h), ju_arg(k, _, _, t), text(t, tt).
// ju_verify_fn(h): function h of the run verifies a token: it decodes one with the signature on, or calls a
// function that does.
.decl ju_verify_fn(h: node)
ju_verify_fn(h) :- ju_decode(c, _), !ju_nosig(c), nearest(c, h, fdef).
ju_verify_fn(h) :- ju_verify_fn(i), call_target(k, i), nearest(k, h, fdef).
// ju_tok(c, tt): tt is the text of the token c decodes (or passes to a helper that does): the argument itself, what
// a name given there was bound to, or a name bound to the argument's expression (`token = creds.credentials`).
.decl ju_tok(c: node, tt: symbol)
ju_tok(c, tt) :- ju_token_arg(c, t), text(t, tt).
ju_tok(c, tt) :- ju_token_arg(c, t), kind(t, "identifier"), text(t, x), look(t, x, h), asg(h, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v),
    text(v, tt).
ju_tok(c, x) :- ju_msrc_fn(c, g), ju_token_arg(c, t), text(t, tt), asg(g, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v), text(v, tt).

// ---- algorithms from the token's header --------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ju_hdr(e): e reads a token's header without verifying it: get_unverified_header(s), `json.loads` of a base64
// decode, or a call of the run's function that returns one.
.decl ju_hdr(e: node)
ju_hdr(c) :- call_name(c, n), (n = "get_unverified_header" ; n = "get_unverified_headers"), docof(c, d), !ju_test_doc(d).
ju_hdr(c) :- call_name(c, "loads"), ju_call_q(c, "json.loads"), ju_arg(c, 0, "", a), has(a, k, "call"), call_name(k, n),
    (icontains("b64", n) ; icontains("base64", n)), docof(c, d), !ju_test_doc(d).
ju_hdr(k) :- ju_hdr_ret(g), call_target(k, g), docof(k, d), !ju_test_doc(d).
.decl ju_hdr_ret(g: node)
ju_hdr_ret(g) :- ju_hdrv(v, _), child(r, v, 0), kind(r, "return_statement"), nearest(r, g, fdef).
// ju_hdrv(e, o): e holds the header read at o.
.decl ju_hdrv(e: node, o: node)
ju_hdrv(e, e) :- ju_hdr(e).
ju_hdrv(p, o) :- ju_hdrv(a, o), child(p, a, _), (kind(p, "parenthesized_expression") ; kind(p, "await")).
ju_hdrv(r, o) :- ju_hdrv(v, o), asg(h, x, v, _), look(r, x, h), kind(r, "identifier"), r != v.
// ju_algv(e, o): e holds the `alg` of the header read at o, unchecked: `header["alg"]`, `header.get("alg")`, a list
// of one, a name bound to one, a parameter a caller passes one to. A value tested with `in`/`==`/`!=` or passed to a
// validator-named call in its function stops it.
.decl ju_algv(e: node, o: node)
ju_algv(e, o) :- ju_hdrv(v, o), field(e, "value", v), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "subscript", k), str(k, "alg"),
    !ju_alg_checked(e).
ju_algv(e, o) :- ju_hdrv(v, o), field(f, "object", v), attr_of(f, v, "get"), field(e, "function", f), kind(e, "call"),
    ju_arg(e, 0, "", k), str(k, "alg"), !ju_alg_checked(e).
ju_algv(p, o) :- ju_algv(a, o), child(p, a, _), (kind(p, "parenthesized_expression") ; kind(p, "tuple") ;
    kind(p, "list") ; kind(p, "set") ; kind(p, "expression_list")).
ju_algv(r, o) :- ju_algv(v, o), asg(h, x, v, _), !ju_name_checked(h, x), look(r, x, h), kind(r, "identifier"), r != v.
ju_algv(r, o) :- ju_algv(a, o), ju_param_at(_, g, a, x), look(r, x, g), kind(r, "identifier").
// ju_alg_scope(h): scope h holds an unverified header (a check of an `alg` passed on to another function is not
// read there: that would make the check depend on the values it stops).
.decl ju_alg_scope(h: node)
ju_alg_scope(h) :- ju_hdrv(v, _), nearest(v, h, fscope).
// ju_checked_text(h, t): scope h tests an expression with text t: a side of `in`/`not in`/`==`/`!=`, or an argument
// of a validator-named call (is_, validate, valid_, check_, ensure_, verify_, sanitize, clean, with a leading `_`).
.decl ju_checked_text(h: node, t: symbol, e: node)
ju_checked_text(h, t, a) :- ju_alg_scope(h), kind(cmp, "comparison_operator"), nearest(cmp, h, fscope),
    (op(cmp, "in") ; op(cmp, "not in") ; op(cmp, "==") ; op(cmp, "!=")), child(cmp, a, _), text(a, t).
ju_checked_text(h, t, a) :- ju_alg_scope(h), kind(k, "call"), nearest(k, h, fscope), call_name(k, n),
    match("_?(is_|validate|valid_|check_|ensure_|verify_|sanitize|sanitise|clean).*", n), ju_arg(k, _, _, a), text(a, t).
// ju_alg_checked(e): the scope around `alg` read e tests an expression with e's text.
.decl ju_alg_checked(e: node)
ju_alg_checked(e) :- ju_hdrv(v, _), (field(e, "value", v) ; (field(f, "object", v), field(e, "function", f))),
    text(e, t), nearest(e, h, fscope), ju_checked_text(h, t, _).
// ju_name_checked(h, x): scope h tests name x itself.
.decl ju_name_checked(h: node, x: symbol)
ju_name_checked(h, x) :- ju_checked_text(h, x, a), kind(a, "identifier").
// ju_param_at(c, g, a, x): call c passes argument a to g's parameter x (`self`/`cls` skipped for a method called
// through an attribute or a constructor).
.decl ju_param_at(c: node, g: node, a: node, x: symbol)
ju_param_at(c, g, a, x) :- ju_algv(a, _), posarg(c, i, a), call_target(c, g), !ju_bound_method(c, g), param(g, x, i).
ju_param_at(c, g, a, x) :- ju_algv(a, _), posarg(c, i, a), ju_bound_method(c, g), j = i + 1, param(g, x, j).
ju_param_at(c, g, a, x) :- ju_algv(a, _), call_arg(c, -1, x, a), call_target(c, g), param(g, x, _).
.decl ju_bound_method(c: node, g: node)
ju_bound_method(c, g) :- call_target(c, g), nearest(g, k, scope), kind(k, "class_definition"), !ju_static(g),
    field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, _).
ju_bound_method(c, g) :- call_target(c, g), def_name(g, "__init__"), field(c, "function", f), !attr_of(f, _, _).
.decl ju_static(g: node)
ju_static(g) :- decorator(g, e), text(e, "staticmethod").
// ju_alg_arg(c, a): a is the `algorithms` argument of decode c.
.decl ju_alg_arg(c: node, a: node)
ju_alg_arg(c, a) :- ju_decode(c, _), ju_arg(c, -1, "algorithms", a).
ju_alg_arg(c, a) :- ju_decode(c, _), ju_arg(c, 2, "", a).
.decl ju_alg_kind(k: symbol)
ju_alg_kind("identifier"). ju_alg_kind("subscript"). ju_alg_kind("call").
// ju_header_alg(c, o): decode c takes its algorithms from the header read at o.
.decl ju_header_alg(c: node, o: node)
ju_header_alg(c, o) :- ju_alg_arg(c, a), ju_algv(a, o).
ju_header_alg(c, o) :- ju_alg_arg(c, a), has(a, u, ju_alg_kind), ju_algv(u, o).

// ---- open algorithm lists ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ju_jose_open(c): a python-jose decode that checks the signature with whatever algorithm the header names.
.decl ju_jose_open(c: node)
ju_jose_open(c) :- ju_decode(c, "jose"), !ju_nosig(c), !ju_alg_arg(c, _), !ju_splat(c).
ju_jose_open(c) :- ju_decode(c, "jose"), !ju_nosig(c), ju_arg(c, -1, "algorithms", v), kind(v, "none").
// ju_pyjwt1_open(c): a PyJWT decode without algorithms in a run on PyJWT 1, which then accepts the header's alg.
.decl ju_pyjwt1_open(c: node)
ju_pyjwt1_open(c) :- ju_decode(c, "pyjwt"), !ju_nosig(c), !ju_alg_arg(c, _), !ju_splat(c), ju_pyjwt1(_).
ju_pyjwt1_open(c) :- ju_decode(c, "pyjwt"), !ju_nosig(c), ju_arg(c, -1, "algorithms", v), kind(v, "none"), ju_pyjwt1(_).
// ju_pyjwt1(e): the run is on PyJWT 1: e calls `.decode()` on what `jwt.encode` returns (bytes in PyJWT 1, a str
// that has no decode in PyJWT 2), directly or through a name; or e, a string in a setup.py, pins PyJWT below 2.
.decl ju_pyjwt1(e: node)
ju_pyjwt1(e) :- ju_encode(e), field(a, "object", e), attr_of(a, e, "decode").
ju_pyjwt1(e) :- ju_encode(e), asg(h, x, e, _), look(r, x, h), kind(r, "identifier"), attr_of(a, r, "decode").
ju_pyjwt1(s) :- file_name(d, "setup.py"), kind(s, "string"), docof(s, d), str(s, v),
    match("(?i)\\s*pyjwt\\s*(\\[[^]]*\\])?\\s*(==\\s*[01]\\.|<\\s*2|<=\\s*1\\.|~=\\s*[01]\\.|>=\\s*[0-9.]+\\s*,\\s*<\\s*2).*", v).
.decl ju_encode(e: node)
ju_encode(e) :- call_name(e, "encode"), ju_call_q(e, q), (q = "jwt.encode" ; q = "jwt.api_jwt.encode").
// ju_weak_algs(c): decode c's algorithms list `"none"` or every algorithm the library has.
.decl ju_weak_algs(c: node)
ju_weak_algs(c) :- ju_alg_value(c, a), kind(a, "call"), call_name(a, "get_default_algorithms").
ju_weak_algs(c) :- ju_alg_value(c, a), has(a, k, "call"), call_name(k, "get_default_algorithms").
ju_weak_algs(c) :- ju_alg_str(c, v), match("(?i)none", v).
// ju_mixed_algs(c): decode c's algorithms mix an HMAC algorithm with a public-key one.
.decl ju_mixed_algs(c: node)
ju_mixed_algs(c) :- ju_alg_str(c, h), match("HS[0-9]+", h), ju_alg_str(c, p), match("(RS|ES|PS)[0-9]+K?|EdDSA|Ed25519|Ed448", p).
// ju_alg_value(c, v): v is decode c's algorithms: the argument, or the value a name given there is bound to.
.decl ju_alg_value(c: node, v: node)
ju_alg_value(c, a) :- ju_alg_arg(c, a).
ju_alg_value(c, v) :- ju_alg_arg(c, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, x), look(a, x, h), asg(h, x, v0, _), unparen(v0, v).
// ju_alg_str(c, v): the algorithms of decode c name v (a string item of a list, tuple or set).
.decl ju_alg_str(c: node, v: symbol)
ju_alg_str(c, v) :- ju_alg_value(c, a), (kind(a, "list") ; kind(a, "tuple") ; kind(a, "set")), child(a, s, _), str(s, v).

// The cases, `cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/`, read as one repository: each line ending in `# caught` is
// reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "app/__init__.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/algorithms.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/algorithms.py"
    .fixture "app/deps.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/deps.py"
    .fixture "app/drf_auth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/drf_auth.py"
    .fixture "app/header_alg.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/header_alg.py"
    .fixture "app/jose_auth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/jose_auth.py"
    .fixture "app/oauth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/oauth.py"
    .fixture "app/reverify.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/reverify.py"
    .fixture "app/routing_auth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/routing_auth.py"
    .fixture "app/sessions.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/sessions.py"
    .fixture "app/tokens.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/tokens.py"
    .fixture "app/trust.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/trust.py"
    .fixture "app/utils.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/utils.py"
    .fixture "app/verifiers.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/verifiers.py"
    .fixture "app/views.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/app/views.py"
    .fixture "tests/test_auth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/tests/test_auth.py"
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":10
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":14
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":22
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":39
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":43
    .expect _ at "app/algorithms.py":47
    .expect _ at "app/deps.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/deps.py":31
    .expect _ at "app/drf_auth.py":17
    .expect _ at "app/drf_auth.py":30
    .expect _ at "app/header_alg.py":20
    .expect _ at "app/header_alg.py":24
    .expect _ at "app/header_alg.py":49
    .expect _ at "app/jose_auth.py":10
    .expect _ at "app/jose_auth.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/jose_auth.py":31
    .expect _ at "app/jose_auth.py":35
    .expect _ at "app/oauth.py":15
    .expect _ at "app/reverify.py":64
    .expect _ at "app/reverify.py":71
    .expect _ at "app/routing_auth.py":40
    .expect _ at "app/sessions.py":6
    .expect _ at "app/sessions.py":11
    .expect _ at "app/tokens.py":19
    .expect _ at "app/trust.py":8
    .expect _ at "app/trust.py":15
    .expect _ at "app/views.py":15
.end

// A second repository on PyJWT 1 (it calls `.decode()` on what `jwt.encode` returns): a PyJWT decode without
// `algorithms` is reported there, and stays silent in the repository above (PyJWT 2 raises).
.test pyjwt_one exactly
    .fixture "legacy/__init__.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/pyjwt_one/legacy/__init__.py"
    .fixture "legacy/auth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/pyjwt_one/legacy/auth.py"
    .fixture "legacy/tokens.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/pyjwt_one/legacy/tokens.py"
    .expect _ at "legacy/auth.py":9
    .expect _ at "legacy/auth.py":13
.end

// A third on PyJWT 1 by its setup.py pin.
.test pyjwt_one_setup exactly
    .fixture "setup.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/pyjwt_one_setup/setup.py"
    .fixture "svc/__init__.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/pyjwt_one_setup/svc/__init__.py"
    .fixture "svc/auth.py" from "../cases/python-security-jwt-unverified/pyjwt_one_setup/svc/auth.py"
    .expect _ at "svc/auth.py":7
.end
